  "name": "Livy, Ab urbe condita, ed. W. Weissenborn and H. J. Müller (Leipzig: Teubner, 1884–1911; public domain), Latin text as digitized by the Perseus Digital Library in its canonical-latinLit repository, file phi0914.phi001.perseus-lat2, whose header credits \"W. Weissenborn\", \"H. J. Müller\", \"Teubner\", \"1884-1911\" (digital file CC BY-SA 4.0)",
  "url": "https://github.com/PerseusDL/canonical-latinLit/blob/master/data/phi0914/phi001/phi0914.phi001.perseus-lat2.xml",
  "section": "Book 22, chapter 51, sections 1–4"
 },
 "source_text": "Hannibali victori cum ceteri circumfusi gratularentur suaderentque, ut tanto perfunctus bello diei quod reliquum esset noctisque insequentis quietem et ipse sibi sumeret et fessis daret militibus, Maharbal praefectus equitum, minime cessandum ratus \"immo ut, quid hac pugna sit actum, scias, die quinto\" inquit \"victor in Capitolio epulaberis. sequere; cum equite ut prius venisse quam venturum sciant, praecedam.\" Hannibali nimis laeta res est visa maiorque, quam ut eam statim capere animo posset. itaque voluntatem se laudare Maharbalis ait; ad consilium pensandum temporis opus esse. tum Maharbal: \"non omnia nimirum eidem di dedere: vincere scis, Hannibal, victoria uti nescis.\" mora eius diei satis creditur saluti fuisse urbi atque imperio.",
 "excerpt_note": "Sections 1–4 of chapter 51, complete. As in the Teubner text, sentences after the first begin in lower case. The Perseus file prints \"et\" (sect. 1) and \"di\" (sect. 4) in italics, apparently words supplied by the editor; they are kept. Perseus's corrections of scanning errors (immo, eam, omnia) are followed. Curly quotation marks are given as ASCII.",
 "macrons": {
  "editorial": true,
  "note": "Macrons are editorial: added by Vocābula, not printed in the edition. Vowel quantities follow the app lexicon (Wheelock / DCC spellings) where the word is in it, and standard dictionary quantities otherwise.",
  "uncertain": [
   "pūgnā: long ū before -gn-, following the app lexicon (DCC pūgna); many dictionaries print pugna.",
   "maior: printed without a macron (the a is short; the first syllable is heavy because of the consonantal i).",
   "Hannibal, Maharbal: Punic names; quantities not marked.",
   "Capitōliō: long ō, the usual dictionary quantity; not machine-checked.",
   "pēnsandum: long ē before -ns-; not machine-checked.",
   "eīdem: long ī in the dat. sg. of īdem; not machine-checked."
  ]
